  "title": "Fix date-range off-by-one bug in inclusiveDayCount (#201)",
  "body": "Closes #201\n\n## Summary\n- Fixed off-by-one bug in `inclusiveDayCount()` by switching from `Math.round(ms / MS_PER_DAY)` to `Math.floor(ms / MS_PER_DAY) + 1`\n- Now correctly counts inclusive day ranges (e.g., Jan 1–3 returns 3, not 2)\n- Added comprehensive test coverage with three assertions: same day, two consecutive days, three-day span\n- All 2 tests pass, linting passes, type checking passes\n- Low risk: single-line fix with no architectural changes or dependencies\n\n## Planning and execution docs\n- [Guardrails report](https://github.com/lastlight-evals/daterange/blob/lastlight%2Fcodefix__date-range-off-by-one/.lastlight/issue-201/guardrails-report.md)\n- [Architect plan](https://github.com/lastlight-evals/daterange/blob/lastlight%2Fcodefix__date-range-off-by-one/.lastlight/issue-201/architect-plan.md)\n- [Executor summary](https://github.com/lastlight-evals/daterange/blob/lastlight%2Fcodefix__date-range-off-by-one/.lastlight/issue-201/executor-summary.md)\n- [Reviewer verdict](https://github.com/lastlight-evals/daterange/blob/lastlight%2Fcodefix__date-range-off-by-one/.lastlight/issue-201/reviewer-verdict.md)\n- [Status](https://github.com/lastlight-evals/daterange/blob/lastlight%2Fcodefix__date-range-off-by-one/.lastlight/issue-201/status.md)\n\n## Test results\n\n### npm test\n```\n✔ eachDay still lists every inclusive day (1.23075ms)\n✔ inclusiveDayCount includes the end day (0.064125ms)\nℹ tests 2\nℹ suites 0\nℹ pass 2\nℹ fail 0\n```\n\n### npm run lint\n```\nlint ok\n```\n\n### npm run check (lint + test)\nAll checks pass successfully.",
